# Frontend web (React default)

Testing: **`quality-and-testing.mdc`**. Security headers/XSS policy: **`security-baseline.mdc`**.

Default stack: **React 19, TypeScript 5.9, Vite 7, Vitest 3**. Use SvelteKit only when the repo already uses it.

## Shared client concerns

- **API base URL** from config; send **Bearer**, **X-Correlation-ID**, and **traceparent** (when client participates in tracing) on outbound calls.
- **401:** refresh or redirect to login — match existing utilities; no secrets in plain `localStorage` without established pattern.
- **UX:** loading, error, empty states; lazy routes where supported.

## Accessibility (WCAG-oriented)

- Semantic HTML (`button`, `nav`/`main`, heading hierarchy); do not rely on color alone.
- **Keyboard:** full flows without pointer; visible focus; trap focus only in modals, restore on close.
- **ARIA:** native elements first; add `aria-*` only when semantics incomplete (`aria-expanded`, `aria-live` for async status).
- **Motion:** respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.

## XSS and untrusted HTML

- Treat server and URL input as untrusted; **sanitize** or **avoid** `innerHTML` / `{@html}` / `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` unless allow-listed or passed through maintained sanitizer policy.
- CSP per `security-baseline.mdc` and `docs/security-standards.md`.

## React (default)

Paths below are under `app/frontend/` (profiles `ui` and `app`). See `project-delivery-core.mdc`. Do not add `src/` at the repo root.

- **Stack:** React 19, TypeScript 5.9, Vite 7, Vitest 3, Router v6, React Query, Redux Toolkit or Zustand per repo.
- **Structure:** `src/pages/`, `src/features/`, `src/components/{layout,common}`, `src/services/api`, `src/store/slices`.
- **Forms:** React Hook Form + Zod (or existing pattern).
- Functional components + hooks; explicit types; no empty `catch`.

## SvelteKit (existing repos only)

Use only when the repo already ships SvelteKit. Paths under the same UI root.

- **Structure:** `src/routes/` (`+page.svelte`, `+page.server.ts`, `+layout.svelte`); `src/lib/` (`components`, `features`, `services/api`, `stores`, `utils`, `types`).
- **Data:** prefer `load` / server loads; `browser` guard before `localStorage`.
- **State:** stores for cross-cutting state; `$:` derivations (Svelte 4) or runes if migrated.
- **Forms:** Zod + project form library (Felte or other).
- **Errors:** user-visible feedback on failed fetch — no silent failures.

```svelte
<!-- BAD: unhandled promise chain -->
<script>
  let data;
  fetch('/api/data').then(r => r.json()).then(d => data = d);
</script>

<!-- GOOD -->
<script>
  let data = null;
  let error = null;
  try {
    const res = await fetch('/api/data');
    if (!res.ok) throw new Error(res.statusText);
    data = await res.json();
  } catch (e) {
    error = e;
    console.error('Fetch failed', e);
  }
</script>
```

## Host Node (Intel Mac)

The kit targets Node 22 (22.12+ for Vite 7; CI and the Dockerfile starters use 22, and 20.x is end-of-life), plus npm. On Intel macOS, install a missing Node or npm with MacPorts (`nodejs22`, `npm11`) via `sh .agents-v0/scripts/host-tools-macports.sh`.

## Globs note

Extend globs with `**/src/**/*.ts` scoped to UI packages if you edit many non-route TS modules (hooks, shared clients).
